# rusticl/kernel: don't hold CL images after launch
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45825 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

After a day long debugging #16741 I found that `QueueContextWithState` keeps the sampler views and shader images of the last launch bound until a later launch replaces them. Each view holds a reference on its `pipe_resource`, so images the application has already released stay alive while their views remain bound.

As mentioned in #16741, exporting a 24 MP raw 8 times in one `darktable-cli` process grows live texture memory (`ASAHI_MESA_DEBUG=bodump`, "Texture") by ~0.9 GiB per export, to 6–8 GiB, freed only at process exit. darktable releases all its `cl_mem`s, rusticl drops all its `Image`s (verified with a debug print in `MemBase::drop`), but the `pipe_resource`s survive.

`GALLIUM_REFCNT_LOG` on the retained textures shows the unmatched references coming from `PipeImageView` and sampler views created in `Kernel::launch`.

With this change texture memory returns to 0 after every export (peak during an export unchanged).

Also from the debugging session: refcount data says that the previous bindings to be released when the next launch rebinds are not released. So a 
review from someone who knows the binding/recycling path well is welcome here.

Fixes #16741, also tagging @karolherbst 

This change was developed with AI assistance (Claude). I have reviewed and tested it and confirm the issue is fixed with this MR.
